; One name, four labels below the zone apex.  c.example. and
; b.c.example. exist only because something below them does: they are
; empty non-terminals, with no records of their own.
;
; So a resolver walking down to a.b.c.example. has a choice about how
; much of the name it puts in each question along the way.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
a.b.c	IN	A	192.0.2.1
